<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pierre-Esprit Radisson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1636–<a href="/years/1710">1710</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Radisson</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pierre-Esprit Radisson was a French coureur des bois and explorer in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-france">New France</a>, born between 1636 and 1640. Captured by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohawk-people">Mohawk</a> raiding party near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trois-rivieres">Trois-Rivières</a> in 1651 or 1652, he was adopted into a Mohawk family, following the custom of adopting young captives to replace lost relatives; after a failed escape he was tortured and saved by his adoptive family. With his brother-in-law Médard des Groseilliers he traded and explored around Lake Superior, and after quarrels with the governor of New France the two entered English service. In 1670 they received a royal charter and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudsons-bay-company">Hudson's Bay Company</a>; Radisson later changed sides between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> more than once.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pierre-esprit-radisson.jpg" alt="Pierre-Esprit Radisson" width="330" height="362" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pierre-Esprit_Radisson.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Those who did not were swiftly executed, and runaways were punished: the recaptured French teenager <b>Pierre-Esprit Radisson</b> had his fingernails pulled out.</blockquote><a href="/societies/haudenosaunee">Social Hierarchy of the Haudenosaunee</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-kingdom">the United Kingdom</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=51.51,-0.13&amp;year=1684" aria-label="London on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4547 381 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Pierre-Esprit Radisson"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4997 651h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4997 651h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=51.51,-0.13&amp;year=1684">What was here in 1684? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
